WEBVTT

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.580
Start a game while the team settles in.

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:06.250
This is Friday Rewind at our fictional company, Northstar

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:07.100
Studio.

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:10.820
The host opens Quick Start and picks 80s trivia.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:13.960
Engage creates a room with a join code and

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.240
a QR code.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.980
Leave this screen up so everyone can join.

00:00:17.885 --> 00:00:19.895
Maya joins on her phone.

00:00:19.955 --> 00:00:22.395
She points the camera at the QR code and

00:00:22.395 --> 00:00:23.675
opens the link.

00:00:23.785 --> 00:00:26.235
The room code is already filled in.

00:00:26.295 --> 00:00:29.595
She types her name, taps join game, and waits

00:00:29.625 --> 00:00:30.575
for the host.

00:00:30.625 --> 00:00:33.025
There is no app to install and no account

00:00:33.045 --> 00:00:33.765
to create.

00:00:33.764 --> 00:00:35.784
Ben joins from his laptop.

00:00:35.884 --> 00:00:37.984
He types the play link with the room code,

00:00:38.084 --> 00:00:39.624
then enters his name.

00:00:39.724 --> 00:00:42.084
Back on the host screen, Maya and Ben are

00:00:42.084 --> 00:00:42.684
ready.

00:00:42.924 --> 00:00:45.434
More teammates join in the background.

00:00:45.564 --> 00:00:47.824
Eight players are now in the room.

00:00:47.924 --> 00:00:50.004
The host starts the first question.

00:00:49.929 --> 00:00:52.579
Each player answers on their own screen.

00:00:52.609 --> 00:00:55.419
Maya picks John Cusack and submits.

00:00:55.449 --> 00:00:57.509
Ben goes for Jon Cryer.

00:00:57.609 --> 00:00:59.539
His answer is in too.

00:00:59.569 --> 00:01:01.629
The host can see how many people have answered

00:01:01.889 --> 00:01:03.819
without calling on anyone.

00:01:03.849 --> 00:01:06.779
Once all eight answers are in, the host shows

00:01:06.879 --> 00:01:07.759
the results.

00:01:07.696 --> 00:01:10.826
John Cusack is right, Maya takes the lead and

00:01:10.826 --> 00:01:13.846
her phone shows her points and first place.

00:01:13.936 --> 00:01:16.406
Press S on the host keyboard to show the

00:01:16.406 --> 00:01:17.786
full scoreboard.

00:01:17.886 --> 00:01:19.766
All eight players are listed.

00:01:19.856 --> 00:01:21.866
Press S again to hide it and bring the

00:01:21.866 --> 00:01:22.946
question back.

00:01:23.046 --> 00:01:24.606
The host controls the pace.

00:01:24.691 --> 00:01:27.171
The game moves on to the next question.

00:01:27.211 --> 00:01:30.611
Players answer and the host reveals the result.

00:01:30.651 --> 00:01:34.751
Before round five, the host opens session, then questions

00:01:34.751 --> 00:01:37.691
and chooses ask next beside a question.

00:01:37.731 --> 00:01:40.451
That choice goes to the front of the queue.

00:01:40.491 --> 00:01:43.371
The next round uses the question the host picked.

00:01:43.281 --> 00:01:46.091
A few more questions keep the room guessing.

00:01:46.171 --> 00:01:49.141
Here are the answers from Rounds 5, 8, and

00:01:49.141 --> 00:01:49.691
10.

00:01:49.771 --> 00:01:52.181
The scoreboard stays out of the way during the

00:01:52.681 --> 00:01:52.971
quiz.

00:01:53.051 --> 00:01:55.481
After 10 rounds, the host brings it back for

00:01:55.561 --> 00:01:57.051
the final standings.

00:01:57.131 --> 00:01:59.421
Maya wins Friday Rewind.

00:01:59.611 --> 00:02:02.571
Everyone can see where they finished.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:03.700
The results stay with the session.

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:06.810
The host opens session then rounds and opens the

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:07.600
report.

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:10.420
It brings the round results together for a closer

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:11.040
look.

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:14.290
Choose print, then save as PDF to keep a

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:15.120
copy.

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:16.590
That is the full flow.

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:19.750
Start a room, invite the team, play together and

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:20.920
keep the results.

00:02:21.159 --> 00:02:23.779
That was a fun flashback to the 80s.

00:02:23.859 --> 00:02:25.859
But the questions can be yours.

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:29.189
Write your own or provide a PDF or some

00:02:29.189 --> 00:02:32.269
text and let the system draft quiz questions for

00:02:32.409 --> 00:02:33.129
your team.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.519
What will you build?

00:02:34.519 --> 00:02:37.229
A quiz about a new project, a tool everyone

00:02:37.379 --> 00:02:39.639
needs to learn or something else.
